    "terminalReason": "completed",
    "text": "Excellent! The bounded stack is fully implemented and tested. Here's a summary:\n\n## BoundedStack Implementation\n\n**Class Structure:**\n- `items`: OrderedCollection holding the stack elements\n- `capacity`: Maximum number of items\n\n**Instance Methods:**\n- `push:` \u2014 adds an object; fails if stack is full\n- `pop` \u2014 removes and returns the top; fails if empty\n- `top` \u2014 returns the top without removing; fails if empty\n- `isEmpty` \u2014 answers true if empty\n- `size` \u2014 answers the number of items\n\n**Creation:**\n- `capacity:` (class-side funnel) \u2014 validates capacity is a positive integer, then initializes\n\n**Error Messages:**\n- `capacity must be a positive integer` \u2014 when creating with invalid capacity\n- `stack is full` \u2014 when pushing to a full stack\n- `stack is empty` \u2014 when accessing/removing from an empty stack\n\n## Test Suite (13 tests, all passing)\n\n**Creation validation:** zero, negative, and non-integer capacities fail properly; valid capacity succeeds\n\n**Size & isEmpty:** correct initial state and tracking through operations\n\n**Push:** increases size correctly; fails when stack is full\n\n**Top:** answers the top element without removing; fails when empty\n\n**Pop:** removes and returns the top; fails when empty\n\n**Comprehensive:** LIFO behavior across multiple operations; can reuse capacity after popping\n\nThe packages are unsaved and ready to file out when you want."
